      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've got a couple of epileptic friends. Adding a warp effect for VRC+ users that's just a great big light causes problems, particularly with users not knowing they even have it on. It's kind of absurd that warp effects still play on avatars that are culled. Even for myself, saying bye to my friends and getting flash banged isn't a pleasant experience.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-01-11T05:45:13.060Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Back in the day, many Avatar creators liked to make their own warp effects, but those were at least tied to their avatar and could be disabled via Safety.\n\nWe are currently able to disable Drones and pretty much all Avatar and Voice for other users in the current VRChat Safety Shield Options. Is there a plan to add support to block others Warp Effects? This should count as Sounds and Particles, but it doesn't as far as I know.\n\nI have friends who take naps or like to relax and meditate in VRChat, and the newest Warp Effect is loud and visually distracting.\n\nThere is already a feedback here for Item visibility, which I believe is in the same category as this one:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-more-safety-option-to-disable-items-visibility\n\nIf we continue down the route of VRChat-provided built-in effects and assets, they should be subjected to the same standard of Safety control that is provided for User Safety. Thank you for reading.",
